[structure_builder] text: Now I'll create a custom tool to perform the rotation operation. I'll use ASE for reading the CIF file and performing the rotation around the specified axis.


[structure_builder] tool_call: create_toolbox_tool args={"code": "from ase.io import read, write\nfrom ase.geometry import find_mic\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\n\ndef rotate_around_center(input_file: str, output_file: str, center_index: int, \n                        distance_cutoff: float, rotation_angle: float, \n                        rotation_axis: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate atoms around a center atom within a specified distance.\n    \n    Args:\n        input_file: Path to input CIF file\n        output_file: Path to output CIF file  \n        center_index: Index of the center atom (0-based)\n        distance_cutoff: Maximum distance from center atom to include in rotation\n        rotation_angle: Rotation angle in degrees\n        rotation_axis: Rotation axis as [x, y, z] vector\n        \n    Returns:\n        dict with success status and message\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read the structure\n    atoms = read(input_file)\n    \n    # Convert to 0-based indexing if needed\n    center_idx = center_index\n    \n    # Get center atom position\n    center_pos = atoms.get_positions()[center_idx]\n    \n    # Find all atoms within the distance cutoff (excluding the center atom itself)\n    positions = atoms.get_positions()\n    vectors = positions - center_pos\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(vectors, axis=1)\n    \n    # Create mask for atoms to rotate (within cutoff and not the center atom)\n    rotate_mask = (distances <= distance_cutoff) & (np.arange(len(atoms)) != center_idx)\n    \n    # Get atoms to rotate\n    atoms_to_rotate = positions[rotate_mask].copy()\n    \n    # Perform rotation using Rodrigues' rotation formula\n    # Normalize the rotation axis\n    axis = np.array(rotation_axis, dtype=float)\n    axis = axis / np.linalg.norm(axis)\n    \n    # Convert angle to radians\n    angle_rad = np.radians(rotation_angle)\n    \n    # Rodrigues' rotation formula: v_rot = v*cos(θ) + (k×v)*sin(θ) + k*(k·v)*(1-cos(θ))\n    cos_theta = np.cos(angle_rad)\n    sin_theta = np.sin(angle_rad)\n    \n    rotated_positions = []\n    for pos in atoms_to_rotate:\n        v = pos - center_pos\n        k_cross_v = np.cross(axis, v)\n        k_dot_v = np.dot(axis, v)\n        v_rot = v * cos_theta + k_cross_v * sin_theta + axis * k_dot_v * (1 - cos_theta)\n        rotated_pos = center_pos + v_rot\n        rotated_positions.append(rotated_pos)\n    \n    # Update the positions in the atoms object\n    new_positions = positions.copy()\n    new_positions[rotate_mask] = np.array(rotated_positions)\n    atoms.set_positions(new_positions)\n    \n    # Write the result\n    write(output_file, atoms, format='cif')\n    \n    return {\n        \"success\": True,\n        \"message\": f\"Rotated {np.sum(rotate_mask)} atoms around center atom {center_index} by {rotation_angle} degrees\",\n        \"atoms_rotated\": int(np.sum(rotate_mask))\n    }", "description": "Rotate atoms around a center atom within a specified distance", "group": "structure_modelling", "tool_name": "rotate_atoms"}
